<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Vientiane</h1><p class="st-meta">1707 CE – 1828 CE · capital Vientiane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The central Lao kingdom formed when Lan Xang split in 1707, destroyed by Siam after King Anouvong's revolt of 1826 to 1828.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/lan-xang">Lan Xang</a>'s succession dispute erupted, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/setthathirath-ii">Setthathirath II</a>, with Vietnamese backing, took power at Vientiane around 1707, while <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Luang Prabang</a> broke away. Vientiane kept the old capital and much of the Lan Xang heritage, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerald-buddha">Emerald Buddha</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom ruled the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mekong-river">Mekong</a> valley and much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorat-plateau">Khorat plateau</a>, but it was weakened by wars with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Luang Prabang</a>. In 1779 the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/thonburi-kingdom">Thonburi Kingdom</a> captured Vientiane and carried off the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerald-buddha">Emerald Buddha</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>, and Vientiane became a Siamese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anouvong">Anouvong</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wat-si-saket">Wat Si Saket</a> and tried to restore Lao power.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1826 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anouvong">Anouvong</a> rebelled against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rattanakosin-kingdom">Rattanakosin Kingdom</a> and marched toward <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a>, but was defeated. In 1828 Siamese armies razed Vientiane, deported much of its population to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khorat-plateau">Khorat plateau</a>; Anouvong was captured and died in captivity in Bangkok. The kingdom was abolished, and Vientiane was refounded under French rule.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-vientiane.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Vientiane" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Vientiane_(1707%E2%80%931828).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1707 CE – 1828 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vientiane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Setthathirath II, Ong Boun, Anouvong</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lao</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/laos">Laos</a>, <a href="/countries/thailand">Thailand</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Viang Chan, Vientiane</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1768&amp;focus=kingdom-of-vientiane" aria-label="Kingdom of Vientiane on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7464 1511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Vientiane lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7784 1767L7756 1697M7784 1767L7753 1923M7784 1767L7754 1922M7784 1767L7894 1880M7784 1767L7788 1713"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7756 1697h0M7753 1923h0M7754 1922h0M7894 1880h0M7788 1713h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7784 1767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vientiane. <a href="/atlas?year=1768&amp;focus=kingdom-of-vientiane">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
